{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1356436-alchemicals-in-the-modern-world","id":1356436,"title":"Alchemicals in the modern world","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Alchemical Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-21T22:28:32-08:00","id":1356436,"title":"Alchemicals in the modern world","content":"So I had a thought. <br /> <br /> Modern-day (America, China, Russia, ASEAN, NATO, Warsaw and all that). So let's say that Alchemicals now exist. And are a thing. Each costing as much as an aircraft carrier... but also not needing as much maintenance or personnel. The books and knowledge on how to create them are on the internet, which also opens up the can of worms that is essence physics. Thaumaturgy and sorcery come first, then minor artifacts. Then over the years, as people learn more and more, they begin to build the Exalted.... <br /> <br /> So I've thought about how it would take for them to make the stuff.... but not how they would deal with the souls. Frankly, in a non-closed environment that isn't autochthon, and without access to Yu-shan, I'm not quite clear on how to deal with souls. <br /> <br /> But anyway, the modern world now has alchemicals! How does this work out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T00:16:48-08:00","id":1356445,"title":"","content":"You will need to specify further.<br /> <br /> A. As written, Alchemicals can only be created in Autochthonia for multiple reasons.<br /> 1. Without the closed soul cycle and obsessive soulgem implantation, it is extremely difficult to determine if a soul is sufficiently heroic to catalyze the exaltaiton without slagging the materials.<br /> 2.Creation requires demiurges, which are created by the Design and will of Autochthon and only within him. 3. Alchemical Creation requires the soul to be in a soul gem. While it may be possible to construct them with the sudden wealth of information (although see B1 below), it requires a live nerve of the maker to actually implant them.<br /> <br /> B. There are numerous secondary requirements<br /> 1. Magical materials don't exist in the real world. While some of them could be created, orichalcum refined into gold, others like starmetal and jade cannot. This limits what alchemicals you can make.<br /> 1.1 Soulsteel is a special case. The only known methods to create new soulsteel require exotic materials from the underworld, and perhaps somewhere in the Maker since he created it originally. The methods are also morally reprehensible. All soul gems require soulsteel spikes at their back and all alchemicals require soul gems.<br /> 2. Alchemicals require vat facilities to create. Normally these are Elder Alchemicals, but that is impossible. Baring that, you can convert a demesne/manse into a vat's facility.<br /> 2.1 There are no dragon lines or demesnes in the real world to convert<br /> <br /> <br /> Assuming these various concerns are handwaved away, the Alchemicals are almost the least disruptive element. Magical materials will revolutionize materials science, demesnes are infinite, renewable clean power that also requires preserving the environment, there are random people being imbued with the demiurgic genius of an absent machine god, and in order to even be able to build alchemicals and their charms entire new industries of magitech must be developed.<br /> <br /> By the time anyone is able to build an alchemical the situation will look very different from the modern real world. Alchemicals are also, comparatively, not worth as much as an aircraft carrier. Even the most combat focused alchemical can only be in one place at a time and is less destructive than a carrier's air wing. Their abilities in stealth and infiltration are impressive, but you can get a lot more for your money with hackers and conventional agents. Even their crafting will be overshadowed by the industry required to build them in the first place.<br /> <br /> They have a few neat toys, like memory reweaving, but at your stipulated price the few groups that can afford them are the ones who least need them.<br /> <br /> Edit: I suppose they might have a unique advantage in their Social charms, but building supernatural demagogues seems dangerous, especially when everyone knows that they can do that. Shards also said that mass media doesn't carry social effects very well, so their revolutionary potential would be limited to in-person speeches.<br /> <br /> <br /> No need to be discouraged though, no doubt someone better informed will be along shortly to refute all of this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 12-22-2019, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T00:37:49-08:00","id":1356448,"title":"","content":"Kinda reminds me of that series with Maise Williams; gen: LOCK produced by Rooster Teeth. Only everyone is on permanent Uptime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T00:44:10-08:00","id":1356449,"title":"","content":"You\u2019d think that if souls were so easy to prove the existence of, there\u2019d be drastically fewer atheists around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T00:59:04-08:00","id":1356451,"title":"","content":"Gods darned it. <br /> <br /> I knew this would be difficult. <br /> <br /> Hmm... Demenses? As infinite energy? I'm not sure. The mote drip they create seems to be rather small. <br /> <br /> Magical materials, I'll give you that such a thing will be very disruptive. <br /> <br /> Though... isn't there a lot more an alchemical can do? Ignoring the social charms, aren't they capable of turning themselves hyperintelligent, and basically competently put in plans and strategies? Would be good for government reform...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T02:26:56-08:00","id":1356457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1356436-alchemicals-in-the-modern-world?p=1356449#post1356449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You\u2019d think that if souls were so easy to prove the existence of, there\u2019d be drastically fewer atheists around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because souls exist doesn't mean that atheists would start worshipping gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T03:06:53-08:00","id":1356459,"title":"","content":"If you want a generic &quot;what happens with superpowers&quot;, see Aberrant. (Or Progenitor.) Or even The Boys (the TV adaptation is pretty cool.)<br /> <br /> Keychain of Creation had a short arc about building Alchemicals in Creation.<br /> <br /> The old Mage: The Ascension source books might be useful for you. In the old World of Darkness, Iteration X rediscovers Autochothonia and uses the technology to build superhuman Cyborgs (including Hit-Marks). The old It-X sourcebooks might be a useful way of capturing Alchemicals in the &quot;real world&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think you're going to need some serious reimagining to make this work. Alita Battle Angel, Ghost in the Shell and the 2004 Casshan movie might all be good inspiration. And, of course, the entire Deus Ex video game series.<br /> <br /> But to scale back your idea a little...<br /> <br /> There's an Exalted Modern wiki idea that might help you -- it's Exalted Modern as Autochothonia: <a href=\"https://rpg.fandom.com/wiki/Exalted_Modern\" target=\"_blank\">https://rpg.fandom.com/wiki/Exalted_Modern</a><br /> <br /> (Alternate, less relevant idea <a href=\"https://rpg.fandom.com/wiki/Modern_Exalted\" target=\"_blank\">https://rpg.fandom.com/wiki/Modern_Exalted</a>)<br /> <br /> Or consider the KoC idea. A single powerful Alchemical breaks into our universe, looking for resources to fix Autochothonia. But is trapped here and can't get back. So she goes full Metropolis (there's a Thor arc where Thor places the city of Asguard in Iowa that might be good inspiration), and starts upgrading the local population.<br /> <br /> Just some thoughts.<br /> <br /> If I may: just building Alchemicals like aircraft carriers off plans found on the internet SPECTACULARLY misses the entire point, and theme, of Alchemicals. I'm not saying &quot;don't do it&quot;, but just like (for example) Burn Legend, you're going to have to reimagine and hand-wave... basically everything about Alchemicals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-22-2019, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T03:29:20-08:00","id":1356461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1356436-alchemicals-in-the-modern-world?p=1356459#post1356459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want a generic &amp;quot;what happens with superpowers&amp;quot;, see Aberrant. (Or Progenitor.) Or even The Boys (the TV adaptation is pretty cool.)<br /> <br /> Keychain of Creation had a short arc about building Alchemicals in Creation.<br /> <br /> The old Mage: The Ascension source books might be useful for you. In the old World of Darkness, Iteration X rediscovers Autochothonia and uses the technology to build superhuman Cyborgs (including Hit-Marks). The old It-X sourcebooks might be a useful way of capturing Alchemicals in the &amp;quot;real world&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> I think you're going to need some serious reimagining to make this work.<br /> <br /> But to scale back your idea a little...<br /> <br /> There's an Exalted Modern wiki idea that might help you -- it's Exalted Modern as Autochothonia: <a href=\"https://rpg.fandom.com/wiki/Exalted_Modern\" target=\"_blank\">https://rpg.fandom.com/wiki/Exalted_Modern</a><br /> <br /> (Alternate, less relevant idea <a href=\"https://rpg.fandom.com/wiki/Modern_Exalted\" target=\"_blank\">https://rpg.fandom.com/wiki/Modern_Exalted</a>)<br /> <br /> Or consider the KoC idea. A single powerful Alchemical breaks into our universe, looking for resources to fix Autochothonia. But is trapped here and can't get back. So she goes full Metropolis (there's a Thor arc where Thor places the city of Asguard in Iowa that might be good inspiration), and starts upgrading the local population.<br /> <br /> Just some thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm.... It's kind of... Different? <br /> <br /> Look. Alchemicals are different. Because they're the only exalts greatly dependent on infrastructure and mortals. They're like ships and tanks and planes. They need to be built and designed, and they need humans to start. <br /> <br /> That's different from aberrant, where eruption can come from anywhere. Or mage the ascension. <br /> <br /> Basically, I'm wondering more about super humans and geopolitics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T04:07:43-08:00","id":1356464,"title":"","content":"Gundam Wing and BattleTech might be good inspiration then.<br /> <br /> I'd recommend looking at The Boys. Set in the modern day, a corporation cracks a genetic engineering drug that gives babies superpowers if you inject them early enough. The drug gets leaked to terrorists. It doesn't have the tech aesthetic of Alchemicals, but it does have the geopolitical angle you want (the USA has corporate sponsored superheroes, and runs a sort of America's Got Talent for their premier super team, liscensed merchandise and movie deals). <br /> <br /> And Deus Ex. Are you sure you don't just want to run Deus Ex?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user